# Google Sign-In (real accounts, via Firebase Authentication + Firestore)
#
# 1. Go to https://console.firebase.google.com and create a project (free).
# 2. In the project: Build -> Authentication -> Get started -> Sign-in method ->
#    enable "Google" as a provider.
# 3. Build -> Firestore Database -> Create database (start in test mode is fine
#    to begin with; tighten security rules before going fully public).
# 4. Project settings (gear icon) -> General -> "Your apps" -> Add app -> Web (</>) .
#    Register the app, then copy the firebaseConfig values below.
# 5. In Authentication -> Settings -> Authorized domains, add your Vercel domain
#    (e.g. your-app.vercel.app) once deployed — localhost is allowed by default.
# 6. Rename this file to ".env" (or ".env.local") and restart `npm run dev`.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
